### Summary

I found nothing that blocks the merge, only two low-severity points, both about the new long-frame names. I read all 20 files and traced the new paths, but ran none of the code or tests. The `telemetry:launchSteps` handler checks the sender the same way as the sibling telemetry handlers, and its failures end in an event sent without steps. The first-run check reads `ao.db` before the daemon can create it, in the same data dir the daemon receives. The Go step payload keys match the PostHog allowlist and its int64 handling. I hand-checked the phase split in `recordLongFrame` against the new unit tests and the arithmetic holds. The two findings are that `invokerName` probably drops `TimerHandler:setTimeout`-style entry points, and that the 40-name cap quietly biases the reported top invoker and bundle without the docs saying so.

